changes.description:
Launch and consume the divider exactly once per valid instruction;
capture forwarded operands for both computation and RVFI. Hold a
completed result under downstream stalls. Distinguish dmem holds
from divider waits: hold EX/MEM only for an unaccepted memory request,
otherwise inject invalid bubbles while the divider runs. Transfer
the original instruction metadata and result to EX/MEM exactly once.

